findings.recommendation:
Add a test with a two-board v8 input where the damage is on the SECOND board, so the assertion can only pass if the loop covers every board. Verified to pass on current code and to fail on the boards[0]-only mutant:

it('damaged fields on the second board are repaired too', () => {
  const b2 = { ...makeV8Data().boards[0], id: 'b2', groupOrder: ['completed', 'completed', 'archive'] } as any;
  b2.groups = fullWidthGroups() as any;
  b2.groups.focus.title = '  ' + 'z'.repeat(45) + '  ';
  const data = makeV8Data();
  data.boards = [data.boards[0], b2];
  const result = migrateData(data);
  expect(result.boards[1].groupOrder).toEqual(['completed', 'backlog', 'focus', 'inProgress', 'orgIntentions', 'delegated']);
  expect(result.boards[1].groups.focus.title).toBe('z'.repeat(40));
});

No mock changes — this is a pure function on plain data.

Add a test that feeds a v8 board with a deleted group key and asserts both no-throw and successful repair. Verified to pass on current code and to fail on the GROUP_IDS-loop mutant:

it('a board missing a group does not throw and is still repaired', () => {
  const groups = fullWidthGroups() as any;
  delete groups.orgIntentions;
  const data = makeV8Data({ groups, groupOrder: ['completed'] });
  expect(() => migrateData(data)).not.toThrow();
  expect(migrateData(data).boards[0].groupOrder).toEqual(['completed', 'backlog', 'focus', 'inProgress', 'orgIntentions', 'delegated']);
});

Use a v8 input specifically: a v<5 input would throw in the pre-existing `version < 5` block, which is out of this task's scope. No mock changes.

Assert against an independent literal so the expectation cannot track the input:

const custom = ['completed', 'delegated', 'orgIntentions', 'inProgress', 'focus', 'backlog'];
expect(sanitizeGroupOrder([...custom])).toEqual(custom);

This also removes the `[...DEFAULT_ORDER].reverse()` indirection, which currently makes the expected value depend on another constant in the file.

Add one non-ASCII boundary case to the existing cap test:

expect(sanitizeGroupTitle('я'.repeat(41))).toBe('я'.repeat(40));
expect(sanitizeGroupTitle('я'.repeat(40))).toBe('я'.repeat(40));

This pins the cap to characters rather than bytes and matches the `maxlength="40"` the input field will use in Task 8, which also counts code units.
